======================================================================
  WHAT THE PARALLEL EVALUATION TEACHES
======================================================================

  T_5: H = 15, I(Omega(T_5), 2) = ... (need conflict graph)
  G_5: H = 10964, I(G_5, 2) = 793
  Note: I(G_5, 2) counts independent sets of ISO CLASSES weighted by 2^k

  OCF CHECK ON G_5 AS DIGRAPH:
  G_5 is a bidirected graph (each undirected edge = 2 directed arcs)
  H(G_5) = 10964 (directed Hamiltonian paths in the bidirected graph)
  This counts paths that can go in either direction along each edge.

  KEY RATIOS:
  H(G_5) / H(T_5) = 10964 / 15 = 730.93
  H(G_5) / 12! = 10964 / 479001600 = 2.288928e-05
  H(T_5) / 5! = 15 / 120 = 0.1250

  E[H] at n=12 (random tournament) = 233887.5
  H(G_5) / E[H](12) = 0.0469
  G_5 has FEWER Ham paths than a random 12-tournament

  INDEPENDENCE POLYNOMIALS:
  I(T_5, x) = 1x^0 + 5x^1
  I(G_5, x) = 1x^0 + 12x^1 + 36x^2 + 38x^3 + 16x^4 + 2x^5
  I(T_5, 2) = 11
  I(G_5, 2) = 793
  I(T_5, x) has all real roots: True
  I(G_5, x) has all real roots: False

  SUMMARY OF PARALLELS AND CONTRASTS:
  T_5 is a tournament (complete, directed, n=5)
  G_5 is a graph (sparse, undirected->bidirected, n=12)

  T_5: H=15 (max possible). Regular. Strongly connected.
  G_5: H=10964. Degree sequence [np.int64(2), np.int64(3), np.int64(3), np.int64(3), np.int64(4), np.int64(6), np.int64(6), np.int64(6), np.int64(6), np.int64(7), np.int64(7), np.int64(7)].
        Connected: True. Kings: 6.

  THE DEEP PARALLEL:
  T_5 is the MAXIMIZER within 5-tournaments.
  G_5 is the STRUCTURE of the space of 5-tournaments.
  Evaluating G_5 with tournament invariants tells us
  about the TOPOLOGY of tournament space itself.
